From 29afe22d1c14805f81b59327885f3f4c1cd287e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:46:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] sccp: force unresolved tops, absorption rules, bounded
 seeding, O(n) phi promotion

Red-team audit of the pass (external review + in-repo verification) found six
defects and left three rules unverified for lack of repo context. This commit
fixes all six, resolves the three from the IR ground truth, and adds one more
hole only the IR could reveal.

Soundness:
- Invariant 5 (latent miscompile): a CondBranch on a value that survives the
  fixpoint as Top marks neither successor; the successor is treated as dead
  and its phi operands pruned, yet the branch is never folded, so the block
  still runs at runtime with a missing phi copy. After every fixpoint,
  force_unresolved_to_bottom lowers every surviving Top visible in an
  executable block to Bottom (conservatively, never to a guessed constant)
  and the solver re-runs; on well-formed SSA this costs one linear scan.
- InlineAsm outputs are definitions that dest() does not cover, so the
  closed default arm never saw them. They are now lowered to Bottom
  explicitly in both seed and evaluate_instruction; previously their
  opacity depended on the accident that the use-def table counts asm
  outputs as uses without a recorded definition.
- seed indexed lattice/use_count/dest ids derived from possibly stale
  metadata (release builds run without the staleness debug_assert): the
  id bound now also covers the largest dest actually present, and every
  seed access is bounds-checked, so a size disagreement degrades to a
  missed optimisation instead of a panic.

Precision (all through the shared constant_fold oracle, guarded on
ty.is_integer() so NaN * 0, -x * 0, NaN - NaN and NaN == NaN can never
fold):
- absorbing zero: x * 0 and x & 0 fold even when x is overdefined
  (GCC CCP / LLVM SCCP both do this; it lets Kconfig-gated branches die
  in the same SCCP run). Covers every integer width plus IrConst::Zero.
- absorbing all-ones: x | -1 == -1, the Or mirror of the zero rule.
  Matched by constructor, never by conversion (I128 truncation to -1 is
  not all-ones).
- same-value identities: x ^ x == 0 and x - x == 0 for identical SSA
  operands; reflexive integer comparisons fold to the canonical boolean
  (Eq/Sle/Sge/Ule/Uge true, the rest false). SCCP runs before
  bit_idioms in the pipeline, so these die one full stage earlier.

Efficiency:
- diagnostic env gates read once per process (OnceLock) instead of five
  getenv paths per function.
- constant-phi promotion is one stable retain + one splice (O(n)); the
  previous remove-in-a-loop was O(phis^2), and pruning allocated a
  survivors Vec per phi even when nothing was pruned (now counted first,
  retained in place).
- the duplicated lattice lookups in materialise/substitute/
  const_of_operand share one lattice_const helper, which also retires
  the _value_type_is_used import-silencing hack.

Tests: 11 new regressions cover every rule above plus the unresolved-Top
diamond (both successors stay executable, nothing pruned) and asm-output
opacity. Units 1706/0/6; regression suite 578/0/15 AB-diff 0;
LCCC-vs-GCC differential 50/0.
